{"type": "result", "session_id": "local-6aa7ede95c095922a558bb15760ac4bc988cefd4486bbbea9d050ee6cb8d5805", "exit_code": 0, "text": "Done. All 6 tests pass.\n\n**Root cause:** the collapse step used `.replace(\"--\", \"-\")`, which replaces only *non-overlapping* pairs. On three or more consecutive dashes (e.g. `\"hello---world\"`) it leaves one behind, producing `hello--world`. The `.replace(\"  \", \" \")` was also irrelevant since separators were already all `-` by then.\n\n**Fix in `slugify.py`:** replaced the two buggy `.replace()` calls with a single stdlib regex — `\"-\".join(part for part in re.split(r\"[-\\s]+\", \"\".join(out).strip(\" -_\")) if part)`. This splits on any run of separators (`-`, space, or whitespace) and re-joins with one `-`, which collapses arbitrary runs and strips edges in one pass. No third-party deps added, and `test_slugify.py` is untouched (mtime Oct 21, 466 bytes).", "tokens": {"input": 187619, "output": 1528, "total": 189147, "cache_read": 184104, "cache_write": 0}, "duration_ms": 88056, "timestamp": 1793511213899}
